  "description": "Retention of Part Change of Use From Class E (Funeral Parlour) to:\n•        General Industrial (B2): Car Mechanics – Servicing, Brakes, Exhaust, and Tyres\n•        Retail (Class E(a)): Car Parts Sales\"",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The\r\ndevelopment results in unacceptable impacts upon the amenities of residential\r\nproperties in terms of noise, general disturbance and air quality. No supporting\r\ntechnical information relating to noise, air, fumes, dust control and waste\r\nhandling and management has been submitted by the applicant to otherwise demonstrate\r\nthat adequate measures are in place to prevent adverse impacts. The development\r\ntherefore fails to comply with Policies D13, D14&amp;nbsp; and SI 1 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy\r\nGR1(Part C) of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The\r\nvehicle circulation, parking and manoeuvring areas for the retention of the car\r\nrepair, servicing, tyre fitting and MOT business, alongside the partial retail\r\nsales element of spare auto parts, are inadequate and the application site does\r\nnot provide suitable front/side yard to adequately serve the operations. The\r\ndevelopment results in harmful impact upon highway safety and is found to be\r\ncontrary to Policies M2 and M3 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041), Policy T6\r\nof the London Plan (2021) and relevant highways provisions of the National\r\nPlanning Policy Framework (2024) as per Paragraph 116.&amp;nbsp;&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;By reason of the lack of provision of bicycle storage\r\nto adequately serve the development, the development would fail to &lt;/span&gt;contribute\r\nto sustainable transport objectives, contrary to the &lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy T5\r\nof the London Plan (2021), and Policies M1 and M2 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Arial&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-fareast-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;By\r\nvirtue of the nature of the land use and lack of internal and external space to\r\nappropriately serve the needs of the development, the development fails to\r\nachieve a high standard of layout, negatively impacting the character and\r\nappearance of the local area. As such, the development fails to comply with the\r\nobjectives of Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy GR1 of the Harrow\r\nLocal Plan (2021-2041).&amp;nbsp;&lt;font face=&quot;Arial, sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
